%9Setting:%9

    backup_auto (off, daily or weekly; default: off)

%9Description:%9

    Backs up the erssi home by itself, once a day or once a week, into
    backup_dir (/HELP backup_dir), the same backup /BACKUP NOW makes
    (/HELP backup). One line in the window of client messages (the
    Notices window of erssi) says where each backup went:

        Backup: ~/erssi-backups/erssi-auto-3f2a91c0-20261101-120000.tar.gz (48 KB)

    The next backup is due a day (a week) after the last one that
    worked. The time of the last one is kept in ~/.erssi/backup-auto.state
    (mode 0600), so a restart or /UPGRADE makes no extra backup, and a
    day missed while erssi did not run is made up a minute after the
    next start.

    A backup that fails is said once, with the reason, and tried again
    an hour later; the same failure again is not said again. /BACKUP
    shows why the last one failed. A backup that runs when erssi quits
    or /UPGRADEs is stopped, and also tried again an hour later.

    With backup_dir inside the erssi home, with no installer installed
    with erssi and in Capsicum capability mode no backup is made, and
    turning the setting on says why.

%9Examples:%9

    /SET backup_auto daily
    /SET backup_auto off

%9See also:%9 BACKUP, BACKUP_DIR, BACKUP_KEEP
